\section{Introduction}
\subsection{Problem Statement and Motivation}

The exponential growth of World Wide Web has created an unprecedented demand for automated data collection tools. Manual retrieval of specific resources—such as documents, multimedia, or datasets—from modern websites is increasingly inefficient due to the sheer volume of data and the complexity of dynamic web technologies. Consequently, the development of intelligent Web Crawlers has become essential for tasks ranging from data archiving to academic research.

In this project, we design and implement a \textbf{Web Crawler}, a high-performance PHP-based application engineered to automate the extraction of multi-format files. This system addresses key challenges in modern web scraping, including handling lazy-loaded content, bypassing basic anti-bot mechanisms, and managing server sessions efficiently to prevent blocking.

